{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers","id":894468,"title":"Alternative Seers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-19T18:01:04-07:00","id":894468,"title":"Alternative Seers?","content":"So I like my villains to be mutli-dimensional, and I do see the Seers as being good antagonists. What I have a minor problem with is that all the background information paints them as selfish and without any kind of the &quot;Well-Intentioned Extremist&quot; angle I usually see in antagonists of their style. Has anyone made efforts in giving them more substance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:05:27-07:00","id":894471,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this complaint keeps coming up.<br /> <br /> The well meaning extremists are at the bottom of the organization. It's just that you can't really buy into Seer ideology and not end up a bastard coated in bastard. Especially if you develop a Prelacy and give the Exarchs a direct line to your soul. There's nothing well meaning about tyranny in its purest form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:10:04-07:00","id":894472,"title":"","content":"They have all the substance of a dictatorship or multinational corporation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:40:01-07:00","id":894485,"title":"","content":"There's two kinds of Seer; the selfish, reward-oriented bastards you seem to be tired off, and the devoted servants of the closest things to gods our world has. I personally enjoy stressing the latter aspect a great deal, as higher-ranking Seers receive visions from the Exarchs themselves. Faith is always a fascinating motivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:09:18-07:00","id":894489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=894485#post894485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's two kinds of Seer; the selfish, reward-oriented bastards you seem to be tired off, and the devoted servants of the closest things to gods our world has. I personally enjoy stressing the latter aspect a great deal, as higher-ranking Seers receive visions from the Exarchs themselves. Faith is always a fascinating motivation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, I forgot that: Theocracies. They do theocracy quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:26:26-07:00","id":894502,"title":"","content":"I don't know tough question. If you wanted too. You might be able to borrow from Ascension? I mean the Technocracy did have a lot more leeway for characterization. As an organization they did kick out a lot of wonder and shut down a lot of magic, but they did solidify and stabilized the world/reality as a whole.<br /> <br /> If I was looking for alternative Seers, The Technocracy isn't a bad way to go. They have dashes of BigBrother and Control. An organization that harnesses the Fabric of Reality to shut out the supernatural believing it too dangerous for mortal man, would make a good counter to a group trying to rise up or escape from the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:27:39-07:00","id":894503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers#post894468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I like my villains to be mutli-dimensional, and I do see the Seers as being good antagonists. What I have a minor problem with is that all the background information paints them as selfish and without any kind of the &quot;Well-Intentioned Extremist&quot; angle I usually see in antagonists of their style. Has anyone made efforts in giving them more substance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use the GoV and accept the fact that the Seers are in fact selfish punks. There isn't any 50 grades of grey silliness going on with them once they actually get 2+ status in their order. After that they receive visions from their God and aren't themselves anymore. Deal with it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise run a MtAw/MtAs hack with either the Seers or Technocracy to your flavor. Seers of the Throne choose that path for good reason. It's because they get serious power just like the Tremere. <br /> <br /> I suppose if you're really serious about a morally grey villain you do a Seer with 2 dots status that's a Tremere Liche.<br /> <br /> For me the irony is delicious how about you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 05-19-2016, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:49:55-07:00","id":894513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=894503#post894503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use the GoV and accept the fact that the Seers are in fact selfish punks. There isn't any 50 grades of grey silliness going on with them once they actually get 2+ status in their order. After that they receive visions from their God and aren't themselves anymore. Deal with it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise run a MtAw/MtAs hack with either the Seers or Technocracy to your flavor. Seers of the Throne choose that path for good reason. It's because they get serious power just like the Tremere.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you're really serious about a morally grey villain you do a Seer with 2 dots status that's a Tremere Liche.<br /> <br /> For me the irony is delicious how about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prelacies only open up at Status 3+, not 2+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:26:42-07:00","id":894531,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm trying to marry the concept of Gakuho Asano from Assassination Class with the concept of a Seer. The idea is an NPC who believes that the weak fear the strong, so he pushes those who follow him to become strong by segregating them from the weak, who are made victims and examples of. This in turn creates a system where those who follow him fear becoming the weak, and push themselves to rigorous extremes all while crushing the 'weaker' class beneath them. I think this has worked well in a sympathetic sense, if only because he believes this philosophy is the best philosophy to protect those beneath him. I'm kind of with Mrmdubois in that those who mean actual good tend to be on the low end of the totem pole.<br /> <br /> ... as a counterpoint though, I tend to believe that you get the worst examples of a group at the top of the totem pole <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Personally, anyways. <br /> <br /> While A Seer is always a slave, they can be a slave for different reasons. Sometimes they are just a slave who believes fighting is pointless - why fight against god? Why not make the most of the world before you, with the rules they've set for you? Serving the gods means making sacrifices, but isn't that what any god asks of their followers? You want a better world, you get it at the whims of the Exarches. You want a world where you are at the top? Whims of the Exarches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 05-19-2016, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T23:35:26-07:00","id":894578,"title":"","content":"Aside from faith, the other big sympathetic motivation is probably fear. <br /> <br /> Like, it's hardly canonical, but I've always like the idea of some seers who justify themselves as being the champions of humanity. The Exarchs stormed heaven, and cast out the Old Gods to remake their world in their (human) image. The Exarch's have allowed us to claim dominion over the earth, they protect us from the horrors of the Shadow and the Underworld and Faerie and, yes, the Abyss. Are they prefect? Fuck no, obviously. But at the very least, they NEED humanity. <br /> <br /> Say the Pentacle actually wins some victories, the Exarchs are weakened. The Supremal is in chaos, and don't all those Old Gods with a few eternities of pent-up vengance have as good a chance as any of ending up on top? What happens to us while the people who have a vested interest in protecting us are no longer securely in charge? <br /> <br /> (Bullshit? Probably, but &quot;even if the status quo is bad, any major change will inevitably lead to things getting much worse&quot; has historically proven to be a compelling argument for the people in charge.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T23:58:55-07:00","id":894587,"title":"","content":"A noble/self-justifying Seer basically believes in the medieval ethos of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_chain_of_being\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Great Chain of Being&quot;</a>. The people at the bottom need to be kept at the bottom and the top at the top because reality itself depends on it. There's a reason that the usurpation of the rightful king in Shakespearean plays results in nature itself being thrown into turmoil.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft (in his cultural-scale social darwinistic racism) dealt with similar themes in &quot;At the Mountain of Madness&quot; and how the rising of the lower (the Shoggoth) cause the degredation that destroys Elder Things civilization.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course for anyone who actually believes in the <i>professed</i> ideals of liberal democracy, it's hard to not see this ideology as inherently villainous, but through much of history it's been taken for granted as a given truth (including by racist misogynists who claimed to believe in liberal democracy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-20-2016, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T00:57:14-07:00","id":894604,"title":"","content":"Elaborating on what glamourweaver said, I think naturalising the Exarchs is a generally valid option. To The Strongest, you actually get a natural explanation for the Exarchs. Maybe also get rid of the Exarchs wanting to conquer the Watchtowers. Even if it's true, they probably shouldn't be admitting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T06:06:55-07:00","id":894681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=894513#post894513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prelacies only open up at Status 3+, not 2+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Because at 3 dots you are catagorically evil. And no amount of philosophy debate will float. At that level you are past the point of no return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T06:08:02-07:00","id":894682,"title":"","content":"Not if you've read The Man Comes Around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:25:48-07:00","id":894734,"title":"","content":"The Seers aren't always capital E evil, but they're never in it for altruism. A lot of them are just selfish sellouts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:55:47-07:00","id":894749,"title":"","content":"I dont necessarily view them all as being evil but they make the counter point of the pentacle mage in regard to their view and approach to magic. The seers wants to be given the answers instead of pursuing mysteries. Which explains theyre relation with the exarch who provides these answer and powers in exchange for obediance. Another point is that they dont care about understanding what magic is and how it really works they just see it as useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:39:34-07:00","id":894906,"title":"","content":"The exarchs and seers remind me a lot of the bad guys from Gurren Lagan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:50:15-07:00","id":894917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=894906#post894906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exarchs and seers remind me a lot of the bad guys from Gurren Lagan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. While the king in the first part, has tried/seen/and failed to uplift, so instead he keeps everything in check. The rock and the hard place. He can't fight the anti-spirals, so he keeps what little of life as safe as possible. Keeping life underground, to hide them from anti-spiral annihilation, but oppressing them as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:41:17-07:00","id":894957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=894681#post894681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. Because at 3 dots you are catagorically evil. And no amount of philosophy debate will float. At that level you are past the point of no return.</div> </div> </div> </div>False. Mystery Commands has Resolution criteria that, while not removing the Prelacy by achieving it, requires the mage to turn on the Exarchs quite decisively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:38:29-07:00","id":895011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=894587#post894587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A noble/self-justifying Seer basically believes in the medieval ethos of the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_chain_of_being&amp;quot;]&amp;quot;Great</a> Chain of Being&amp;quot;[/URL]. The people at the bottom need to be kept at the bottom and the top at the top because reality itself depends on it. There's a reason that the usurpation of the rightful king in Shakespearean plays results in nature itself being thrown into turmoil.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft (in his cultural-scale social darwinistic racism) dealt with similar themes in &amp;quot;At the Mountain of Madness&amp;quot; and how the rising of the lower (the Shoggoth) cause the degredation that destroys Elder Things civilization.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course for anyone who actually believes in the <i>professed</i> ideals of liberal democracy, it's hard to not see this ideology as inherently villainous, but through much of history it's been taken for granted as a given truth (including by racist misogynists who claimed to believe in liberal democracy).</div> </div> </div> </div>What is interesting is the Diamond uses the same logic in why they fight the Seers: the Exarchs are not the rightful rulers of the Supernal, as beings who took the Heavens by force, and therefore reality itself isn't what it should be. Hence the Lie and Paradox. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the need for Villians, the best groups are often the Pentacle. The Orders have enough greatness that they support outright black, who often are those who embraced their missions (or at least part of their Order's ethos) too much. Here are some examples:<br /> - An arrow who creates conflict to gain challenges, or creates oaths that drives him to darkness.<br /> - A Silver Ladder who &quot;just can't get people to see the way&quot; and thus forces them to. <br /> - A Guardian who no longer knows who they once were as they cycle through Masques, or who no longer trusts any Mage as he has seen them all fail to many times. <br /> -A free council Mage who is now a terrorist, not a freedom fighter, or who harms sleepers because &quot;he doesn't believe anything should be kept from them, even if it may be painful&quot; and thus exposes them to the shard of the abyss by actively using magic in front of them. <br /> -A Mysterium Mage who claims that the only way to protect magic is to purge sleepers, or who willingly sacrificed sleepers and mages so as to be taught magical secrets by one of the bound which he fears may otherwise be lost for all of time. <br /> <br /> Another group is the Scelesti. Serving the Anti-reality has actually less of an obvious evil, even if it is truly worse than a Seer. An example from 1e is a Aswadim (an Archmage sworn to the Abyss) who seeks <i>to destroy all of the Shadow</i>. Why? Because he wants to replace it with a version he created and raised from the Abyss that would create a Shadow that is not predatory amongst its denizens, but instead a positive community, and have this false Shadow in turn act to make humanity better. It sounds truly noble, and he turned to such a solution as he saw no other way to fix the Shadow with the the vast, God-like powers he had as an Archmage. He is also friendly and overall a decent guy(God?), even towards those who hinder him (to a point... He isn't a pushover.) It doesn't mean he should actually be supported though, but he can make players question themselves.<br /> <br /> As for the Seers themselves, the &quot;best&quot; morally gray ones are the &quot;believers&quot; and the &quot;fearful.&quot; <br /> <br /> -Having those who truly believe that the Exarchs are Divine and thus serve from belief makes their actions somewhat harder to call out. I mean, can you truly fault someone who not only believes they are doing the work of the gods, but can actually point to their servants (Ochema), their influence and active control, and their issuance of commands for choosing to serve such beings? It may mean they do horrible things, but they truly believe that they are doing an actual God's will. <br /> -The &quot;fearful&quot; Seer plays into this a bit to, and can overlap as well. A true believer would also fear their God's wrath, which unlike modern religion, they can actively see the Exarchs moving in the world and know that they will punish those (either via Ochema or other Seers) those who displease them, or worse, actively work against them. Even someone who doesn't see them as gods could rightly argue that the Seers are powerful, and that they would rather live in luxury and not fear some cosmic beings displeasure, even if that means serving a tyrant, than face the risk of such beings noting them and directing their wrath upon them.<br /> <br /> Mixing the fearful and faithful seers in can make them somewhat more gray; both are selfish in a way but one that can make someone at least understand their motives. Just don't forget the ones drawn to the Seers cause they like power and want to be on the &quot;winning team&quot; either, or that even those who are faithful or fearful seers are going to engage in dark stuff in service of their lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T15:39:18-07:00","id":895050,"title":"","content":"Mmmmm... The Diamond are aligned with the Oracles not the Old Gods. The Silver Ladder still sees mass Ascension as a worthy goal. So no, I don't agree that they're reactionaries who want an older hierarchy restored (as a group anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:08:34-07:00","id":895086,"title":"","content":"I feel like it would be easy to spin a character that started as a Pentacle Mage and was like &quot;man these guys are fighting an unwinnable war against Gods and sure are causing a lot of collateral damage/deaths...also those Seers are sort of guarding one of the Bound and keep it from fucking everyone up...maybe I'm on the wrong side&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:26:34-07:00","id":895105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=895050#post895050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmmm... The Diamond are aligned with the Oracles not the Old Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Alleged</i> Oracles.<br /> <br /> It is my understanding that no mage has met or interacted with these purported Oracles or even their ochemata. The Oracles are just a very <i>convenient </i>explanation for some mage awakenings (which include Seers).<br /> <br /> The myth of the Oracles merely serves to placate the consciences and assuage the guilt of weak and hubristic Pentacle mages. I guess fools will cling to any hope, no matter how false, rather than face the Truth.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs always won, are winning, and will forever win. The Exarchs are the Supernal, and the Supernal are the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Pentacle mages claim to see through the Lie, yet they still clearly deceive themselves.<br /> <br /> Why remain an inmate in the prison of the Lie and needlessly suffer when you can rule and prosper. Why fight a war already lost before time even began?<br /> <br /> Join the Seers, embrace the world and true reality, and reach your full potential.<br /> <br /> --- Tetrarch Belial, Ministry of Mammon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-20-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:27:20-07:00","id":895108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=895050#post895050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmmm... The Diamond are aligned with the Oracles not the Old Gods. The Silver Ladder still sees mass Ascension as a worthy goal. So no, I don't agree that they're reactionaries who want an older hierarchy restored (as a group anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oracles are often portrayed as being the true kings of Atlantis, the Exarchs usurpers who took power and seized the Ladder and then the Supernal, and that the Oracles fought them to push back their influence. And most of the time the idea of Ascension isn't being portrayed as a Mass Ascension (unless you are talking to some in the Silver Ladder) but instead that the Supernal shouldn't be hidden and those who achieve the right to Ascend should be able to do so should (same with awakening).) And some archmages do choose to serve the old gods out of the idea they are restoring the rightful rulers, though that is fuzzier. Though most of this is 1e lore, and it can be interpreted differently. It also is a bit of a Tangent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:01:28-07:00","id":895147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=895105#post895105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Alleged</i> Oracles.<br /> <br /> It is my understanding that no mage has met or interacted with these purported Oracles or even their ochemata. The Oracles are just a very <i>convenient </i>explanation for some mage awakenings (which include Seers).<br /> <br /> The myth of the Oracles merely serves to placate the consciences and assuage the guilt of weak and hubristic Pentacle mages. I guess fools will cling to any hope, no matter how false, rather than face the Truth.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs always won, are winning, and will forever win. The are the Supernal, and the Supernal are the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Pentacle mages claim to see through the Lie, yet they still clearly deceive themselves.<br /> <br /> Why remain an inmate in the prison of the Lie and needlessly suffer when you can rule and prosper. Why fight a war you already lost before time even began.<br /> <br /> Join the Seers, embrace the world and true reality, and reach your full potential.<br /> <br /> --- Tetrarch Belial, Ministry of Mammon</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I'm sold. I notice this is the Ministry of Mammon, do I have to buy in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:17:57-07:00","id":895162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=895147#post895147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I'm sold. I notice this is the Ministry of Mammon, do I have to buy in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't think of it as anything so base and mundane as a &quot;buy in.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are a mage, a wolf among the sheep, a visionary among the blind and ignorant, a prince among serfs and peasants.<br /> <br /> Consider yourself as entering the most exclusive and lucrative executive training program in all of reality.<br /> <br /> Will there be some sacrifices and costs. Of course, nothing in life is free, and the weak, lazy and stupid are not fit to rule. However the rewards and benefits, both magical and temporal, are beyond compare, and they only get bigger and better and you move on up.<br /> <br /> Are you prepared to take what is rightfully yours?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-20-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:48:31-07:00","id":895178,"title":"","content":"I made a thread about trying to make different Seers. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/829033-heroic-seers\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...3-heroic-seers</a> People posted some great and fun things in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:59:34-07:00","id":895184,"title":"","content":"As much as I'm liking the new edition of mage, I'm also having trouble with this. For all it's idealism the pentacle is flawed, you can find some real nasty bastards in their ranks and I love it, but the seers? They're just selfish assholes who have sold themselves. They know it, don't care about it, and even rub it in your face. I was really hoping that they wouldn't make it so obvious in the new edition.<br /> One thing that you could do, and it's what I choose when I run a game, is this: The abyss is the result of a massive magical catasthrope due to the abuse of magick. The world had to be severed from the supernal to trap the abyss between both and that way prevent reality being swallowed by the abyss. Now, who did cause the catasthrope and who saved the world? That's where both factions disagree. The pentacle says that the exarcs created the abyss to rule a non magical humanity as absolute tyrants, the oracles are the heroic rebels trying to give humanity a fighting chance. The seers say that exarcs are the ones working tirelesly to keep both worlds safe from the abyss while they try to fix it. The pentacle is nothing but a bunch of ignorant anarchists working for a group of power hungry terrorists that don't care about destroying reality as long as they can get to the top. Who's right and who's wrong? Who knows? Perhaps they are even both right, or both wrong, you decide.<br /> It's just a matter of making the setting your own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T18:58:50-07:00","id":895218,"title":"","content":"Another awesome Seer motivation comes from the flavor quote from my favorite Legacy, The Quiescent: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;It's not a Lie. It's a governing principle of the world, and we should just get used to it.&quot; </div> </div> </div>To the Seers, the Pentacle is fighting a war that literally ended before the beginning of time. The Exarchs have sat on their thrones for the entirety of this reality's existence and nothing is likely to ever dislodge them; the Supernal has likewise been parted from the Fallen by the Abyss, and the Lie is as much a part of being human as any other possible descriptor. Dreams of mass Awakening or a return to Atlantis are pleasant fantasies, but utterly unlikely of ever coming true. No one has struck down even the least of the Exarchs over the span of human history, and the only grow more powerful every single day.<br /> <br /> Why not serve the winning team and enjoy the ride? It's not a matter of being a selfish asshole or a divinely-inspired zealot, it's a matter of facing the facts and not throwing your life away chasing deluded idealism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:22:35-07:00","id":895229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=895218#post895218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not serve the winning team and enjoy the ride? It's not a matter of being a selfish asshole or a divinely-inspired zealot, it's a matter of facing the facts and not throwing your life away chasing deluded idealism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> Also, the whores and drugs are really top shelf! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T20:47:45-07:00","id":895264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=894917#post894917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. While the king in the first part, has tried/seen/and failed to uplift, so instead he keeps everything in check. The rock and the hard place. He can't fight the anti-spirals, so he keeps what little of life as safe as possible. Keeping life underground, to hide them from anti-spiral annihilation, but oppressing them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd argue that the anti-spiral races are also similar to the Exarchs. What happened the last time that humanity had unfettered access to supernal power? The world ended so hard they had to make a new one. Sure, it was the Exarchs who did the deed and the ones who benefit the most, but do you think the common man would be better served by a bunch of other mages following them up there and making war?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T23:56:35-07:00","id":895352,"title":"","content":"Well the Seers are right. Their bosses are at the top of the universe, in a very static way. They aren't the good guys for sure, but to me they aren't any worse than your typical warlord or autocrat. I sort of view them as swords and sandals sorcerer princes mixed with Illuminati types. The way the cosmos is set up you couldn't expect anything else, and unlike real governments or societies their doesn't seem to be any route for change.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the Seers can be interesting and sympathetic even if you don't take my view of them. Plenty of historical dramas are about tyrants and people root for them anyways. Cesare Borgia would be my go to. The guy is the definition of Machiavellian, but very interesting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:41:49-07:00","id":896117,"title":"","content":"Something on being evil bastards is that you can be an evil bastard without being a nasty evil bastard. The Seers don't want to kill everyone on Earth, for instance (like some Mysterium did in the early 20th Century). And a big factor of their MO is taking out extrawordly beings that try to kill everyone and binding the Chthulus they don't like.<br /> <br /> It's still ultimately self-serving motivations (&quot;the Exarchs don't want to rule a kingdom of ashes&quot;) but it is something that makes them at least not quite as 100% black as say, cWoD Nephandus or some Left-Handed Legacies about.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:06:06-07:00","id":896131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896117#post896117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something on being evil bastards is that you can be an evil bastard without being a nasty evil bastard. The Seers don't want to kill everyone on Earth, for instance (like some Mysterium did in the early 20th Century). And a big factor of their MO is taking out extrawordly beings that try to kill everyone and binding the Chthulus they don't like.<br /> <br /> It's still ultimately self-serving motivations (&amp;quot;the Exarchs don't want to rule a kingdom of ashes&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but it is something that makes them at least not quite as 100% black as say, cWoD Nephandus or some Left-Handed Legacies about.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. I think the grey comes from the fact that the Seers acts as a powerful force in blocking powerful entities, Bound, Gulmoths, Acamoths, and possibly others when it interfers with their plans, so at times that could mean the God Machine, True Fae, powerful spirits, ect...<br /> <br /> And purpusing the interests of their Exarch can mean doing good things.<br /> <br /> Like a Seer of Mammon might try and boost the local economy, in order to connvince the local sleepers that capitalism can solve their problems, a Seer of Unity might support universal healthcare and other universal social programs in order to file off some individuality, but it would see help millions of people in need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:09:17-07:00","id":896132,"title":"","content":"I'm really confused on how people can claim that Seers aren't that bad. Flat out says that, even if someone joined out of misguided altruism, they're quickly disabused of that notion. You're either in it for the power, or because you're too scared to run away. Or both. There's no shades of grey here. Doing the occasional &quot;stop the other evil thing&quot; does not suddenly redeem the Seers, or make them less evil. It just means that they get to go on oppressing, hurting, killing, and abusing others.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is why I focus on the so-called Left Handed Mad, Scelesti and Reapers for my antagonists. Much more in the way of nuances and depth to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:14:50-07:00","id":896137,"title":"","content":"Personally I can see Unity being the Greyest of the Exarchs, the most tempting to the generous.<br /> <br /> Still Seers are still human, and as, such only a minority or going to be full on pyschopaths, the rest rationalize their asses off or seek to buy off their sins with good works in their spare time.<br /> <br /> A Seer of the General might sell weapons to competing governments, but donate alot of money to war orphans and victims of war rape as a way to cope with feeling of guilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:12:36-07:00","id":896172,"title":"","content":"Except not. You're working for the embodiments of oppression specifically because you want the benefits. Seers are like the politicians or corporate fat cats at the top who sit there and lie, twist, decieve, oppress and maniupate the people so they can remain in power and get richer. These are people who will hear about wounded veterans that can't get in to see doctors, shrug, and go on with out a care. They dehumanize and dismiss people all the time, so long as they can remain in power. Look at the Flint water crisis. Sure, you might call that the act of a few psychopaths. Except that kind of situation is coming up across America. Its not a localized issue, its a wide spread one.<br /> <br /> Don't underestimate the apathy of the powerful towards the less fortunate. Sure, they're not psychopaths. Psychopaths are people with a genetic predisposition; there's a reason for their methods and madness. You don't need to be a psychopath to dehumanize and oppress others. And that's exactly the attitude the Seers cultivate. Look at the sample picture of the Seers. Torture for entertainment. That's not the exception. That's the default.<br /> <br /> You want to help out orphans? <i>You are a bloody mage</i>. You don't need to sell weapons. Simple spells, like Fate or Mind, to earn some money and donate it. You sell weapons because you want the money, then make up excuses why you're not evil. Guess what? Very few people admit to being evil - its a common psychological defense to say that you're not evil, but justified. <i>That doesn't excuse the evil actions</i>.<br /> <br /> This isnt' Robin Hood here. This is the Sheriff of nottingham throwing a few coins to peasants as he rides past, nevermind that the tax collectors will snap up that money back in a little bit, and it still leaves the peasants in a state of abject poverty. And donating to orphans is a tax write off anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-22-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:15:00-07:00","id":896173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896172#post896172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except not. You're working for the embodiments of oppression specifically because you want the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or worse-because it's easy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:20:44-07:00","id":896180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896172#post896172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You want to help out orphans? <i>You are a bloody mage</i>. You don't need to sell weapons. Simple spells, like Fate or Mind, to earn some money and donate it. You sell weapons because you want the money, then make up excuses why you're not evil. Guess what? Very few people admit to being evil - its a common psychological defense to say that you're not evil, but justified. <i>That doesn't excuse the evil actions</i>.<br /> <br /> This isnt' Robin Hood here. This is the Sheriff of nottingham throwing a few coins to peasants as he rides past, nevermind that the tax collectors will snap up that money back in a little bit, and it still leaves the peasants in a state of abject poverty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why Seers as written don't work for me as a faction. The &quot;standard Seer&quot; is an interesting singular antagonist, but a whole faction of people who know that they are evil and their masters are evil and their job is evil and their ultimate goal is evil? That's little..too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:24:20-07:00","id":896183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896172#post896172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except not. You're working for the embodiments of oppression specifically because you want the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or because the alternative is worse. Remember what happened last time someone tried to remove those symbols? Reality itself Broke.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:33:53-07:00","id":896187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896183#post896183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or because the alternative is worse. Remember what happened last time someone tried to remove those symbols? Reality itself Broke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually thats a problem. no one know really knows why Uptopia broke apart. We have ideas, but no defining proof.<br /> <br /> What we do know. There might have been, possibly in the future, but definatly not here, perfect place. and then something happened or didn't happen to it.<br /> next ???<br /> now our present situation is thus. The world is twisted, and the only gods up there answering the phone, are tranytical in nature. Meanwhile being are waking up to the imperfect nature of the world around them, without a defined answer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:41:49-07:00","id":896191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896173#post896173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or worse-because it's easy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Same thing, when you get down to it. Benefits don't necessarily have to be tangible, and sloth is just a valid of a vice as any other.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896183#post896183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or because the alternative is worse. Remember what happened last time someone tried to remove those symbols? Reality itself Broke.</div> </div> </div> </div> False dichotomy. The alternative is <i>not getting involved in the war at all</i>. Go Nameless. Join an Order but don't get involved in anything major while focusing on research. The book is pretty clear on the matter that people who join out of misguided altruism are quickly disabused of that notion; there is no &quot;this is better than the alternative&quot; when it comes to working with the Seers. Even if you don't want to get involved with the war against oppression, there are alternatives to joining the oppressors. <br /> <br /> And lets not forget that the 11th Exarch specifically cultivates the Abyss like a garden. If not for that particular Seal, the Abyss may very well have mended. And that the whole Time Before is now an unclear Mystery - we don't know if the Exarchs were Atlantean mages anymore, or not. If there was a Celestial Ladder, if the Oracles are a thing, or not. There's no evidence that reality broke because of a war against the Exarchs. And even if it was true? The Abyss was the direct result of climbing into the Supernal with bodies from the Phenomenal World via Ladder, mixing the pure and impure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:42:49-07:00","id":896192,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm not Anarchist enough to like Seers enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:13:13-07:00","id":896211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896191#post896191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is <i>not getting involved in the war at all</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And implicitly allow what the Pentacle wants to do? As in, recreate the world before the Fall, where casuality doesn't necessarily follow a linear pattern, where <i>anyone</i> get reality-bending powers (which, IMO, is akin to having toddlers play with live grenades)? No thanks, I like the laws of physics nice and stable.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book is pretty clear on the matter that people who join out of misguided altruism are quickly disabused of that notion; there is no &quot;this is better than the alternative&quot; when it comes to working with the Seers. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and again IMO, this makes them boring characters. This is why I choose not to focus on that part.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if you don't want to get involved with the war against oppression, there are alternatives to joining the oppressors. </div> </div> </div>If you're not part of the solution...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And lets not forget that the 11th Exarch specifically cultivates the Abyss like a garden. If not for that particular Seal, the Abyss may very well have mended. </div> </div> </div>I fail to understand why this is a good thing. Again, the comparison to kids with explosives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:18:17-07:00","id":896213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896211#post896211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and again IMO, this makes them boring characters. This is why I choose not to focus on that part.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not &quot;part.&quot; That's kind of the whole. You want to change the game, sure, have fun. But please don't portray it as if its cannon. The book made it very clear that what you want is not part of the Seers at all, nor are you accurately representing the Pentacle alliance, but reducing it to a characture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:27:26-07:00","id":896264,"title":"","content":"I don't think most Seers categorize themselves as &quot;evil&quot;. First of all, I don't think Mages so easily categorize themselves as evil / good in the first place, because the notion instantly clashes with at least some of the Paths. A Mastigos would scoff at the notion, and an Obrimos doesn't care what you call him: he's got his purpose and has seen God eye-to-eye, etc.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium takes property from Sleepers, the Guardians keep them blindfolded, the Silver Ladder uses them as pawns, the Free Council patronizes them, the Arrows don't even care except when it helps them &quot;prove&quot; themselves by protecting them. So, the Pentacle is pretty evil in many ways. The difference is that the Seers say, &quot;You know, let's cut the bullshit, we gotta do this thing and not fake we are the good guys, that's silly.&quot;<br /> <br /> The world is filled with &quot;evil&quot; people. Banks that steal from their customers. Industries that destroy the environment. Politicians that rewrite law to their benefit. And all of this is possible through the concerted effort of thousands of people, and the great majority will not stop to say, &quot;Whoa, I am being so evil, perhaps I should stop this.&quot; Most of them are worried about providing for their families, improving their lifestyle, even constructing a legacy, or just getting a feeling that they have achieved something and that their life was not for naught. A few will probably realize that they ARE the bad guys (or at least working for them) but they will be like, &quot;Yeah, perhaps this is a little gray area, but its me or them and you always gotta look for number one.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the Seers. Orders come from up high and you carry them out. Magic is the paycheck for a job well done. Always be closing, always be looking for your next promotion, fall in line, learn to be always on the winning team, use any means you can and someday, you can be promoted to GOD. Yes, get promoted to fucking GOD of whatever little niche you want.<br /> <br /> The Seers are the perfect antagonist because they hit so close to home, to smacking the player in the face with the realization that, hey, maybe you could be a Seer of the Throne too, and if you don't think you could be them... well, they got a place for people like you too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","user":"arthexis","date":". 05-22-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:28:18-07:00","id":896266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896180#post896180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why Seers as written don't work for me as a faction. The &quot;standard Seer&quot; is an interesting singular antagonist, but a whole faction of people who know that they are evil and their masters are evil and their job is evil and their ultimate goal is evil? That's little..too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;There is no good or evil. There is only power, and those too weak to seek it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:34:00-07:00","id":896520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896213#post896213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not &quot;part.&quot; That's kind of the whole. You want to change the game, sure, have fun. But please don't portray it as if its cannon. The book made it very clear that what you want is not part of the Seers at all . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a big fan of this opinion that seems to crop up whenever someone wants to make slight tweaks to elements of the game. There's room for some interpretation in both the 1e and 2e core regarding how dastardly the Seers are, and changing it so that it's possible to have higher status Seers who find something principled in keeping the world Fallen doesn't rupture some load bearing pylon in the concept of the order. Just like playing an Obrimos who doesn't believe in a higher power or a Thyrsus who isn't a hedonist or environmentalist isn't forbidden in the 'cannon' game.<br /> <br /> There's even some justification, pointed out by Freemind, for Prelates to not be simple &quot;fuck you buddy, I got mine&quot; style tyrants. Prelates <i>scare</i> the unchosen rank and file Seers because they've let their patron start re-shaping their soul. That can be debauched tyranny at a metaphysical level, but it can just as easily mean becoming the embodiment of parochial altruism in the service of the Unity.<br /> <br /> I think it would be perfectly in keeping with not just the theme, but also the vast majority of the Seer aesthetic, to have the Wisdom trait change for a Prelate so that it represented something like Faith in, or Honour to, the patron which chose them, meaning that the Seers could have their own equivalent of Enlightenment, a meshing of their vision with the Exarchs, whose ultimate motives are unfathomable, but who's actions and power derive from the symbols of unchallenged rule. <br /> <br /> If you then treat some of what the book says about the Exarchs as Pentacle propaganda or hearsay, you can create an Order almost identical to the 'cannon' Seers that nonetheless might hold some appeal to idealistic Mages. A story hook for Archmage Tetrarchs in Imperial Mysteries even opened the possibility that the Exarchs were using the power of oppression and tyranny to keep humanity safe from the Old Gods and that the Lie was actually &quot;the Lie of reason, faith and hope that keeps humanity alive.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:33:28-07:00","id":896551,"title":"","content":"I don't see why they need to be &quot;altruistic&quot; to be sympathetic. <br /> <br /> If you look at Game of Thrones ( I am just talking about the TV Show, not the books its simpler). The vast majority of characters have very &quot;grey&quot; moral character by most people's standards. The most popular character in the series is a patricide and woman killer. The magic users are all really scary people who don't seem to give a shit if it gets in the way of their goals. <br /> <br /> And the one &quot;altruistic&quot; guy in the show, is fairly terrifying villain!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:05:22-07:00","id":896591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896551#post896551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why they need to be &quot;altruistic&quot; to be sympathetic.<br /> <br /> If you look at Game of Thrones ( I am just talking about the TV Show, not the books its simpler). The vast majority of characters have very &quot;grey&quot; moral character by most people's standards. The most popular character in the series is a patricide and woman killer. The magic users are all really scary people who don't seem to give a shit if it gets in the way of their goals.<br /> <br /> And the one &quot;altruistic&quot; guy in the show, is fairly terrifying villain!</div> </div> </div> </div>Parochial altruism is pretty double edged actually. It's altruistic in the sense that you're willing to die for your tribe, but the parochial part is just as important: you're willing to die for your tribe trying to kill members of another tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:59:16-07:00","id":896724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sufferian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896520#post896520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a big fan of this opinion that seems to crop up whenever someone wants to make slight tweaks to elements of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> And I'm not a fan of people portraying their personal takes as if it was cannon. Did I say they shouldn't run Seers that way? No. I said that they were <i>changing the Seers and presenting the new form as if it was how the book described it</i>. If the person in question merely said, &quot;This is how I run Seers,&quot; or something similar, there wouldn't be a question. <br /> <br /> The 2e Seer section literally says that people do not join for altrusitic reasons, and those who are misguided are quickly disabused of the notion. Trying to present Seers as altruistic is a direct contradiction of what's written.<br /> <br /> You want to change things, I'm all for it. I encourage it. I've even have writeups in other threads on how to do that very thing. But its disingenuous to portray those changes as if they were the default. You are changing the game. Own it, and go ahead with it. Don't jump into a conversation about the core book Seers with your houserules as if its cannon portrayal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you then treat some of what the book says about the Exarchs as Pentacle propaganda or hearsay, </div> </div> </div> In other words, if you ignore what the book actually says because you don't like it. That's fine, but don't pretend that its the same organization anymore. Its not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:53:32-07:00","id":897535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sufferian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896591#post896591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Parochial altruism is pretty double edged actually. It's altruistic in the sense that you're willing to die for your tribe, but the parochial part is just as important: you're willing to die for your tribe trying to kill members of another tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually another excellent reason to join the Seers, and one you see a lot with people involved in organized crime and similar fields.<br /> <br /> The world is shit. The world has been and always will be shit for the vast majority of people, trying to usher in some grand cosmic revolution is basically quixotic and mainly liable to get people hurt. Trying to care about the entire world is an excellent road to despair or various forms of suicide (there's a very good reason Saints tend to end up as martyrs).<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean you have to just give up. Sure, you can't solve old age or disease, but your mother's going to get the best care money can buy and then some. Poverty's here to stay, but no lover or child of yours is ever going to worry about missing meals or not having a roof over their head. And maybe prison and the courts are here for a reason, but you can make sure that dear friend doesn't get railedroaded on trumped up possession charges because the prosecutor needs to bump up their average. <br /> <br /> Do you have to get your hands dirty doing it? Sure, but everything you do, someone else would have if you didn't. Is it really so much better to sit on the sidelines and declare yourselves the moral victor while everyone you care about starves and suffers? You're Awakened, you're being offered a seat at the table, to be one of the people the system works for. Are abstract principles really worth more than all of your friends and family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T05:26:23-07:00","id":897703,"title":"","content":"An excellent justification, right up until the Exarchs demand you kill your loved ones (Like in the fiction of the Seers book). Probably works for most though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:26:00-07:00","id":897735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896551#post896551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why they need to be &quot;altruistic&quot; to be sympathetic.<br /> <br /> If you look at Game of Thrones ( I am just talking about the TV Show, not the books its simpler). The vast majority of characters have very &quot;grey&quot; moral character by most people's standards. The most popular character in the series is a patricide and woman killer. The magic users are all really scary people who don't seem to give a shit if it gets in the way of their goals.<br /> <br /> And the one &quot;altruistic&quot; guy in the show, is fairly terrifying villain!</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The idea that one must be a 'Well-Intentioned Extremist' to have depth and substance was a flawed one to begin with. As is the idea that being 'disabused' of ones notions of altruism is a path that lacks similar depth. Walter White is a modern character with a lot of depth and substance who quickly realized the harm his plot arc was causing to others and kept with it.<br /> <br /> As popular as the antihero is, there's nothing wrong with villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:29:33-07:00","id":897742,"title":"","content":"I wonder, if everyone is trying to push Seers away from systems of oppression when they game, are the way the Seers depicted in the book the actual way that they're generally portrayed in game? Seems to me that people want to push the Seers in the same direction that the old Technocracy went.<br /> <br /> Well, I personally think that the Seers are reminants of the whole Traditions V. Technocracy Ascension war in the first place, and I alter them to fit into a more investigative angle than they currently occupy. I don't want a war for reality, I want a game about investigating strange things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-24-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:42:12-07:00","id":897750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=897703#post897703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An excellent justification, right up until the Exarchs demand you kill your loved ones (Like in the fiction of the Seers book). Probably works for most though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that loved one was also a Seer herself. She brought that one on herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:50:50-07:00","id":897798,"title":"","content":"The Seers Don't have the Rationalization Bent that the Techs had or the Technological progressiveness. The Seers kept the oppression and dialed it up. Both groups are keeping the world intact, but by different imperatives. The Techs removed mythicism because of its erratic effects to the whole, and hope to actualize mankind as a whole. What and How that actualization takes is still up for debate. The Seers keep the lie in motion for reasons we dont know. Obviously to keep themselves in power and privilege(same with techies but to a different degree) and by the directive, thats the way its always been. and that mind set is continually reinforced by jailors to be. The world is already pretty oppressive, and its not going anywhere anytime soon. Sign up for the pay. and remember Corporate Loves You.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:02:12-07:00","id":908723,"title":"","content":"Not certain if someone has mentioned this before but...<br /> <br /> If you have the patience for it (and few do) but the film 'Beyond the Black Rainbow', I imagine, would be excellent inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8160-squidbat","name":"Squidbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8160_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T20:18:48-07:00","id":912060,"title":"","content":"So for unrelated reasons I was watching Jesus Christ, Superstar. And it struck me that if you keep the Seer organization, or at least the Exarch's, as malevolent as in canon you could create a sympathetic, or at least interesting, Seer off total agreement that the Exarch's are horrific, evil gods who keep humanity chained and tortured for their own amusement. All it takes is a couple close encounters with Ochemeta and a realization of what they could do to any large group of humans who go from amusing to threatening. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g-voeq7Cebo\" target=\"_blank\">Or to quote Judas</a> <br /> <br /> <i>Listen, Jesus, do you care for your race?<br /> Don't you see we must keep in our place?<br /> We are occupied<br /> Have you forgotten how put down we are?<br /> <br /> I am frightened by the crowd<br /> For we are getting much too loud<br /> And they'll crush us if we go too far.<br /> If we go too faaaar<br /> <br /> Listen Jesus to the warnign I give<br /> Please remember that I want us to live<br /> But it's sad to see our chances weakening with every hour<br /> Your followers are blind<br /> Too much Heaven on their minds</i><br /> <br /> A similar sort of character would be Stephen Colbert's at the end of his episode in the last season of Rick and Morty. Tyrannizing the people of his world out of a certainty that it exists for the convenience of a higher reality, and that should it cease to be convenient it will cease to exist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T03:01:30-07:00","id":912174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=897750#post897750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but that loved one was also a Seer herself. She brought that one on herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>A <i>failing </i>Seer even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T08:09:44-07:00","id":912237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=912174#post912174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A <i>failing </i>Seer even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. She wouldn't have brought it on herself if she hadn't gotten complacent and lazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:57:35-07:00","id":912315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896117#post896117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">like some Mysterium did in the early 20th Century</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you meant by that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:16:26-07:00","id":912337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=912315#post912315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you meant by that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Daksha are basically magical racists who supported the Third Reich, though since the Germans and their allies weren't also magical hermaphrodites they'd probably have stepped up the purification program eventually.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium is also the Order that probably cares for the Sleepers the least (Even less than Seers). Sleepers degrade magic that's in their presence and spread Pancryptia in spite of themselves. The fact that they can't help it doesn't stop a number of members of the Mysterium from being bitter about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:19:59-07:00","id":912340,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't like &quot;shades of grey&quot; villains. I like scary villains, who will do really repulsive things. I like driven villains; who are sure they are right and you are wrong. I like villains who take our values and corrupt and perverse them until we look at them and wonder how we ever thought whose ideals were a good idea. Seers are just those villains. Corrupt corporate executives, bloodthirsty warlords, oppressive government bureaucrats, hypocritical priests. Dark sides of human nature, taken to the extreme and supported with ability to warp reality - now that is scary and repulsive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:32:40-07:00","id":912348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=912340#post912340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like villains who take our values and corrupt and perverse them until we look at them and wonder how we ever thought whose ideals were a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's pretty much what shades of grey in a villain are supposed to evoke. Well that or they can actually tempt the heroes to join in their corruption. The trope is simply supposed to evoke enough humanity that a person can look at it and say that it's horrible while also seeing that without caution they could end up going down the same rabbit hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:48:04-07:00","id":912354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=912348#post912348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's pretty much what shades of grey in a villain are supposed to evoke. Well that or they can actually tempt the heroes to join in their corruption. The trope is simply supposed to evoke enough humanity that a person can look at it and say that it's horrible while also seeing that without caution they could end up going down the same rabbit hole.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't that I meant. For example, we universally think that helping others is a good thing, right? Yet there is a Seer, whose work is to shepard hungry low-lifes, until they are utterly dependant on him and his pylon. Unity in people is good, until Seers hatch a plan of turning Sleepers into united, mindless horde of faceless cattle. There is no need for &quot;we could end up the same&quot; trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:55:48-07:00","id":912391,"title":"","content":"Sure, there are Seers who would hatch such a plan merely for the evilness of it, but it could happen just as easily to a well-meaning FC cabal by accident. They start helping people, not realizing the dependency that they're building up in them. I mean it's fine, you don't have to have the concern that you could end up the same as the villain and that's going to come down to the ST deciding how the setting reacts to the actions of the players anyway. I'm not even arguing for shades of grey as much as point out hey, from the example you've given it's remarkably easy to work in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:26:36-07:00","id":913576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896724#post896724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I'm not a fan of people portraying their personal takes as if it was cannon. Did I say they shouldn't run Seers that way? No. I said that they were <i>changing the Seers and presenting the new form as if it was how the book described it</i>. If the person in question merely said, &quot;This is how I run Seers,&quot; or something similar, there wouldn't be a question.<br /> <br /> The 2e Seer section literally says that people do not join for altrusitic reasons, and those who are misguided are quickly disabused of the notion. Trying to present Seers as altruistic is a direct contradiction of what's written.<br /> <br /> You want to change things, I'm all for it. I encourage it. I've even have writeups in other threads on how to do that very thing. But its disingenuous to portray those changes as if they were the default. You are changing the game. Own it, and go ahead with it. Don't jump into a conversation about the core book Seers with your houserules as if its cannon portrayal.<br /> <br /> In other words, if you ignore what the book actually says because you don't like it. That's fine, but don't pretend that its the same organization anymore. Its not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because for me and it looks like others, the Seers <b><i>as written</i></b> are useless because of the stuff that you bring up. I normally say the same thing about the Pure. They are evil in the same way as a Captain Planet villian. They are just to hive minded to be believable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:29:50-07:00","id":913581,"title":"","content":"Kind of unlikely for people only looking out for themselves to be hive minded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:24:17-07:00","id":913626,"title":"","content":"As someone who never watched Captain Planet the analogy doesn't really work. Hell, in the few clips I've seen of it, the villains are pretty coherent in their motives, making profit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:40:01-07:00","id":913887,"title":"","content":"I think that trying to find multidimensional character traits by looking at the Order's beliefs might be looking at the problem the wrong way. <br /> <br /> From what I've observed all of the Orders have rather flat, easy to recognize traits that each Caucus and Cabal shares over all. My belief is that they're built that way on purpose so that regional and personal interpretations can allow Storytellers and Players to make organic social groups by exploring their themes trough play. <br /> <br /> At their core, the Seers of the Throne covet temporal power almost as much as they crave Supernal might. Their strength is linked to exploiting reality's limitations so they have the highest quality tools available and their Hubris is thinking that they can get away with it without consiquences so long as they are cleaver enough. What Mages, or for that matter Mortals in general, would not only accept that set of beliefs but also thrive in such a cutthroat hierarchy? How will their actions shape their Path? And what of the Supernal Symbols they pledge themselves to serve? Is Magic truly payment for exploiting those around you? Or is it payment for creating the very Gods they serve? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:18:03-07:00","id":945971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896724#post896724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I'm not a fan of people portraying their personal takes as if it was cannon. Did I say they shouldn't run Seers that way? No. I said that they were <i>changing the Seers and presenting the new form as if it was how the book described it</i>. If the person in question merely said, &quot;This is how I run Seers,&quot; or something similar, there wouldn't be a question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, sorry it's taken me so long to get back to you, I only visit these forums periodically! But, to return to this argument which is probably sort of pointless by now . . . I wasn't trying to imply that you were telling people how to run their game. My impression was just that you thought that small variations within the scope of the cannon were somehow against that cannon. I think I see you doing that here as well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896724#post896724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, if you ignore what the book actually says because you don't like it. That's fine, but don't pretend that its the same organization anymore. Its not.</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument was that it would be the same organization, but my interpretation of that organization differs slightly from the author's. There's lots of authorial statements throughout nWoD that contradict each other to some extent, and sometimes this is even done on purpose. If you change all of the little things I plan to change with the Seers of the Throne, you end up with a slightly different organization. But if you just change it so that there's one or two high Wisdom Seers kicking around, I don't think that makes them completely different. And, finally:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/894468-alternative-seers?p=896724#post896724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2e Seer section literally says that people do not join for altrusitic reasons, and those who are misguided are quickly disabused of the notion. Trying to present Seers as altruistic is a direct contradiction of what's written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a Seers of the Throne organization that was altruistic would be an entirely different organization. Unfortunately, if you read what I've written, that's not what you'll find. And, in fact, you'll find something that's in agreement with a lot of the way Seers of the Throne operate: conditional co-operation with an in-group or tribe, violent opposition to arbitrarily determined opponents, i.e. parochial altruism. When you open your soul up to a God of Tyranny, you sort of start looking less like a &quot;fuck you buddy, I got mine&quot; and start looking more like someone who has dedicated themselves to a fanatical cause.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}